name: the long tail
after: 09-sed
intro: Counting and summarising a corpus you did not write -- which is most of
intro: what triage actually is. Everything here reads learn's own shipped files,
intro: so the answers are real and the tree is yours to measure.
---
setup: Every shipped command has one page under /usr/share/learn/ref, one file
setup: per command.
q: count how many commands learn documents in /usr/share/learn/ref
a: ls /usr/share/learn/ref | wc -l
a: ls -1 /usr/share/learn/ref | wc -l
ref: ls
cmp: ref
hint: one filename per line out of ls, then count the lines
---
setup: find prints one path per line under /usr/share/learn, so it counts by
setup: piping into wc.
q: count every regular file under /usr/share/learn
a: find /usr/share/learn -type f | wc -l
ref: find
cmp: ref
hint: -type f picks files only, skipping the directories find also lists
---
setup: Each ref file's first line is the command's own name.
q: print the first line of every file under /usr/share/learn/ref, sorted
a: sed -n '1p' /usr/share/learn/ref/* | sort
a: head -qn 1 /usr/share/learn/ref/* | sort
why: live-hw
ref: sed
hint: sed -n '1p' prints only line 1 and stays silent on the rest
